# Test Execution and Gradle Integration

## Gradle Command Construction
Always use the cross-platform Gradle wrapper approach:

```python
import platform
import subprocess

# Detect OS and select appropriate wrapper
gradle_cmd = "gradlew.bat" if platform.system() == "Windows" else "./gradlew"
gradle_cmd = os.path.join(project_root, gradle_cmd)

# Build command with test class
cmd = [
    gradle_cmd, "test",
    f"--tests={test_class_name}",
    "--info",
    "--stacktrace",
    "--offline"
]
```

## Test Execution Pattern
```python
try:
    result = subprocess.run(
        cmd,
        cwd=project_root,
        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
        stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
        text=True,
        timeout=300,  # 5 minutes
        check=False
    )
    
    # Process results
    if result.returncode == 0:
        logger.info(f" Test {test_class_name} passed")
        state["execution_passed"] = True
    else:
        logger.error(f" Test {test_class_name} failed")
        state["execution_passed"] = False
        
except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
    logger.error(" Test execution timed out")
    state["execution_passed"] = False
except FileNotFoundError:
    logger.error(" Gradle wrapper not found")
    state["execution_passed"] = False
```

